nsure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-799cf069-368d-5fad-8ff3-f06fd1cc93a6" :question/id #uuid "799cf069-368d-5fad-8ff3-f06fd1cc93a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-34483" :question/problem "How is the angle $-\\frac{17\\pi }{9}$ normally represented in the coordinate plane?" :question/worked-solution "To help us to visualize the angle, we first convert the measure of the angle into degrees. \n\nTo convert the measure of an angle in radians to an equivalent measure in degrees, we multiply the measure in radians by $\\frac{{180}^{∘}}{\\pi }.$ This gives\n\n$$\n-(\\frac{17\\pi }{9})\\cdot (\\frac{{180}^{∘}}{\\pi })=-{340}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nSo, the angle $-\\frac{17\\pi }{9}$ is equivalent to $-{340}^{∘}.$ \n\nNow, we recall that:\n\n- An angle in the standard position has its initial side on the positive $x$-axis, and a vertex that lies at the origin.\n\n- It rotates such that a positive angle is measured counter-clockwise, and a negative angle is measured clockwise.\n\nTherefore, the correct diagram is as follows:\n\n![](images/a8/a82ca9d59a88071320c95a78d10900c73c32e4c156dddb32a57603121923b8c5.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-bac22063-b3ae-514c-8d0f-7f5b7583523c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-bac22063-b3ae-514c-8d0f-7f5b7583523c" :answer-field/id #uuid "bac22063-b3ae-514c-8d0f-7f5b7583523c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8ea4aaed-66ce-5922-998e-3232609aab0f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-aad8519d-75b0-5101-8c2f-f3cf9bfa42fe" "answer-b2a921c8-951d-5b17-91a6-3d9c69e8bf13" "answer-5ae87006-12e8-5ce8-b74c-a345ed296b95" "answer-8ea4aaed-66ce-5922-998e-3232609aab0f" "answer-72c4de8d-b6cf-5dde-bc6c-7dcded79efe7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aad8519d-75b0-5101-8c2f-f3cf9bfa42fe" :answer/id #uuid "aad8519d-75b0-5101-8c2f-f3cf9bfa42fe" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/7c/7c8c0b85a8c06e4f92a7bcf558a6de7c409e4dbbec25b46780d67a8324488250.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b2a921c8-951d-5b17-91a6-3d9c69e8bf13" :answer/id #uuid "b2a921c8-951d-5b17-91a6-3d9c69e8bf13" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/8b/8b22828130202b99c388fdb3b57ad4e311fa67182ca7ffa303ccac2687d45e9c.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5ae87006-12e8-5ce8-b74c-a345ed296b95" :answer/id #uuid "5ae87006-12e8-5ce8-b74c-a345ed296b95" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/99/99d898f557dddfbc28359f705170cfcdedbee9a18dc4d26fd960a6747a79ab7f.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8ea4aaed-66ce-5922-998e-3232609aab0f" :answer/id #uuid "8ea4aaed-66ce-5922-998e-3232609aab0f" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/a8/a82ca9d59a88071320c95a78d10900c73c32e4c156dddb32a57603121923b8c5.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-72c4de8d-b6cf-5dde-bc6c-7dcded79efe7" :answer/id #uuid "72c4de8d-b6cf-5dde-bc6c-7dcded79efe7" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/fa/fa3ed2c1d0b882ec193db83df166b0e27990d9fb8e7e23ede8634b660fd6c53d.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186060878 :tutorial/content "Recall that, in the coordinate plane, an angle $\\theta$ in the standard position has its vertex at the origin, its initial side lies along the positive $x$-axis, and it rotates such that a positive angle is measured counter-clockwise.\n\nSince a positive angle is always measured counter-clockwise, this means that a negative angle is measured *clockwise*.\n\nFor example, we can represent the angles $\\theta = -45^\\circ, -135^\\circ, -225^\\circ,$ and $-315^\\circ$ as central angles of the unit circle (in the standard way) as follows:\n\n![](images/0b/0b33ba078eecacd9f8d40622fb21be5ec710a22b6e69458006c5d9422441285a.png)" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186060879 :tutorial/content "Sometimes, we wish to represent negative angles in the coordinate plane without reference to the unit circle.\n\nAs with positive angles, the convention for representing negative angles is the same as without the unit circle.\n\nFor example, we can represent the angles $\\theta = -45^\\circ, -135^\\circ, -225^\\circ,$ and $-315^\\circ$ in the coordinate plane in the standard way as follows:\n\n![](images/01/019d5fc186f3c540702951b08d8dfcaf67cb82333a6c18a466dc21794e6dc94c.png)" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186059895 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186095676 :answer-field/choices 17592186095680] [:db/retract 17592186095676 :answer-field/choices 17592186095681] [:db/retract 17592186095676 :answer-field/choices 17592186095677] [:db/retract 17592186095676 :answer-field/choices 17592186095678] [:db/retract 17592186095676 :answer-field/choices 17592186095679] [:db/retract 17592186095688 :answer-field/choices 17592186095689] [:db/retract 17592186095688 :answer-field/choices 17592186095690] [:db/retract 17592186095688 :answer-field/choices 17592186095691] [:db/retract 17592186095688 :answer-field/choices 17592186095692] [:db/retract 17592186095688 :answer-field/choices 17592186095693] {:db/id 17592186096720 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-948c8637-9616-53cf-93bb-0432892cbe59"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186097292 :question/problem "A cat’s position relative to a fixed origin $O$ is given by the function $x(t)=3{t}^{2}+t$ meters, where $t$ is the time in hours. Find the average position of the cat between $2$ and $4$ hours." :question/worked-solution "To calculate the average value of the position on $[{t}_{1},{t}_{2}],$ we use the average value formula\n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{{t}_{2}-{t}_{1}}\\,{\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}x(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{4-2}\\,{\\int }_{2}^{4}(3{t}^{2}+t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{({t}^{3}+\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2})|}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[({4}^{3}+\\frac{{4}^{2}}{2})-({2}^{3}+\\frac{{2}^{2}}{2})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[(64+8)-(8+2)] \\\\  & =31.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the average position is $31\\,\\text{m}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186095676 :answer-field/correct "answer-42d18385-9cde-5883-ac5a-37781eda6692" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e90ae4b7-57a0-56d4-b078-d5b219cd95b1" "answer-42d18385-9cde-5883-ac5a-37781eda6692" "answer-04edbe72-2860-5445-9b78-8c22cc20067e" "answer-f81b9df8-fff8-5d97-9c34-430dd36b2e04" "answer-b4d8c80f-bf74-5759-9834-cd33f9e368f1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e90ae4b7-57a0-56d4-b078-d5b219cd95b1" :answer/id #uuid "e90ae4b7-57a0-56d4-b078-d5b219cd95b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-42d18385-9cde-5883-ac5a-37781eda6692" :answer/id #uuid "42d18385-9cde-5883-ac5a-37781eda6692" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "31\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-04edbe72-2860-5445-9b78-8c22cc20067e" :answer/id #uuid "04edbe72-2860-5445-9b78-8c22cc20067e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "32\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f81b9df8-fff8-5d97-9c34-430dd36b2e04" :answer/id #uuid "f81b9df8-fff8-5d97-9c34-430dd36b2e04" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{31}{2}\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b4d8c80f-bf74-5759-9834-cd33f9e368f1" :answer/id #uuid "b4d8c80f-bf74-5759-9834-cd33f9e368f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{63}{2}\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096719 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-c00bebe5-d517-59a2-a7ee-fce25fbbc516"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186097294 :question/problem "A train is moving north-east with velocity $v(t)=6{t}^{2}+8t+100\\,\\text{km/h},$ where $t$ is the time in hours. Find the average velocity of the train on the interval $t\\in [1,4].$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the average value of the velocity on $[{t}_{1},{t}_{2}],$ we use the average value formula\n\n$$\n{v}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{{t}_{2}-{t}_{1}}{\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{4-1}\\,{\\int }_{1}^{4}(6{t}^{2}+8t+100)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(2{t}^{3}+4{t}^{2}+100t){|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}((2(4)^{3}+4(4)^{2}+100(4))-(2(1)^{3}+4(1)^{2}+100(1))) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}((128+64+400)-(2+4+100)) \\\\  & =162.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the average velocity is $162\\,\\text{km/h}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186095688 :answer-field/correct "answer-b0d18fe2-8169-5eb1-b785-85e842c937f8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-81eb2493-7567-5c70-bfd8-ceecf2a4addb" "answer-7e5d16bc-cb25-52d2-b98e-5bb7f17439e1" "answer-b0d18fe2-8169-5eb1-b785-85e842c937f8" "answer-c0e9b334-945a-5161-b29a-cb81ea2bb950" "answer-44246c94-6d8c-5f04-baa0-79045398a988"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-81eb2493-7567-5c70-bfd8-ceecf2a4addb" :answer/id #uuid "81eb2493-7567-5c70-bfd8-ceecf2a4addb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "158\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7e5d16bc-cb25-52d2-b98e-5bb7f17439e1" :answer/id #uuid "7e5d16bc-cb25-52d2-b98e-5bb7f17439e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "160\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b0d18fe2-8169-5eb1-b785-85e842c937f8" :answer/id #uuid "b0d18fe2-8169-5eb1-b785-85e842c937f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "162\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c0e9b334-945a-5161-b29a-cb81ea2bb950" :answer/id #uuid "c0e9b334-945a-5161-b29a-cb81ea2bb950" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "164\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-44246c94-6d8c-5f04-baa0-79045398a988" :answer/id #uuid "44246c94-6d8c-5f04-baa0-79045398a988" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "166\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096718 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5f1c0a58-fb01-5814-8e30-7c47e655e50c"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-5f1c0a58-fb01-5814-8e30-7c47e655e50c" :question/id #uuid "5f1c0a58-fb01-5814-8e30-7c47e655e50c" :question/math-academy-id "q-353938" :question/problem "A robotic rover moves in a straight line with velocity \n$v(t)=3{t}^{2}-t,$ where $t$ is measured in seconds and $v$ is measured in meters per second. \n\nFind the average acceleration ${a}_{\\text{avg}}$ of the rover over the time interval $t\\in [0,2].$ Do not round your answer.\n\n${a}_{\\text{avg}}=$ \n{{field-1}}\n${\\text{m/s}}^{2}$" :question/worked-solution "The average acceleration is the average rate of change of the velocity, so\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{v(b)-v(a)}{b-a} \\\\  & =\\frac{v(2)-v(0)}{2-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{[3(2)^{2}-2]-[3(0)^{2}-0]}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(12-2)-0}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{2} \\\\  & =5\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the average acceleration is $5\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-82e292da-04ee-55d1-86e2-4a2230088d1d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-82e292da-04ee-55d1-86e2-4a2230088d1d" :answer-field/id #uuid "82e292da-04ee-55d1-86e2-4a2230088d1d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-12b4a368-f228-50e0-a65e-e556685ce4e9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-12b4a368-f228-50e0-a65e-e556685ce4e9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-12b4a368-f228-50e0-a65e-e556685ce4e9" :answer/id #uuid "12b4a368-f228-50e0-a65e-e556685ce4e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-c00bebe5-d517-59a2-a7ee-fce25fbbc516" :question/id #uuid "c00bebe5-d517-59a2-a7ee-fce25fbbc516" :question/math-academy-id "q-354478" :question/problem "A small rover moves along a straight track with velocity \n$v(t)=\\sqrt{t}+2,$ where $t$ is measured in seconds and $v$ is measured in meters per second.\n\nFind the average velocity ${v}_{\\text{avg}}$ on the interval $[1,4].$ Do not round your answer.\n\n${v}_{\\text{avg}}=$ \n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{m/s}$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the average value of the velocity on $[{t}_{1},{t}_{2}],$ we use the average value formula\n\n$$\n{v}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{{t}_{2}-{t}_{1}}{\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{4-1}{\\int }_{1}^{4}(\\sqrt{t}+2)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{(\\frac{2}{3}{t}^{3/2}+2t)|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[(\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 8+8)-(\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 1+2)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[(\\frac{16}{3}+8)-(\\frac{2}{3}+2)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\frac{40}{3}-\\frac{8}{3}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{32}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{9}\\,\\text{m/s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the average velocity is $\\frac{32}{9}\\,\\text{m/s}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8d89cc03-11cb-5a33-a4d3-defd63d2cbf9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8d89cc03-11cb-5a33-a4d3-defd63d2cbf9" :answer-field/id #uuid "8d89cc03-11cb-5a33-a4d3-defd63d2cbf9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-561dec26-edfd-5f06-be74-04ce011e37e6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-561dec26-edfd-5f06-be74-04ce011e37e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-561dec26-edfd-5f06-be74-04ce011e37e6" :answer/id #uuid "561dec26-edfd-5f06-be74-04ce011e37e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{32}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-948c8637-9616-53cf-93bb-0432892cbe59" :question/id #uuid "948c8637-9616-53cf-93bb-0432892cbe59" :question/math-academy-id "q-354500" :question/problem "A particle’s acceleration in ${\\text{m/s}}^{2}$ is given by the function $a(t)=\\sqrt{t},$ where $t$ is the time in seconds.  \n\nFind the average acceleration ${a}_{\\text{avg}}$ of the particle on the interval $[1,4].$ Do not round your answer.\n\n${a}_{\\text{avg}}=$ \n{{field-1}}\n${\\text{m/s}}^{2}$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the average value of the acceleration on $[{t}_{1},{t}_{2}],$ we use the average value formula\n\n$$\n{a}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{{t}_{2}-{t}_{1}}{\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}a(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{4-1}{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\sqrt{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{(\\frac{2}{3}{t}^{3/2})|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[(\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 8)-(\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 1)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{16}{3}-\\frac{2}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{14}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{9}\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the average acceleration is $\\frac{14}{9}\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2ab3c0e2-4bdc-50da-b2cf-5a837a9baa2c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2ab3c0e2-4bdc-50da-b2cf-5a837a9baa2c" :answer-field/id #uuid "2ab3c0e2-4bdc-50da-b2cf-5a837a9baa2c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-5859ef23-64ea-5f95-8062-f7664d1b6145" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5859ef23-64ea-5f95-8062-f7664d1b6145"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5859ef23-64ea-5f95-8062-f7664d1b6145" :answer/id #uuid "5859ef23-64ea-5f95-8062-f7664d1b6145" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{14}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-b6659aa2-fce6-56a0-9a42-d00a9aa7628c" :activity/id #uuid "b6659aa2-fce6-56a0-9a42-d00a9aa7628c" :activity/title "Average Position, Velocity, and Acceleration" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048976 :activity/course 17592186046645 :activity/steps ["step-2ccbe3d6-2634-5637-9466-9ccd96f0e3f1" "step-33ff57a1-4ad9-5365-8370-762afd29d628" "step-c74051f2-6f31-5a23-b00a-9ba4cba0db56" "step-5ae097ca-dfcf-58c0-b026-e053a35b47c0" "step-403b655a-e00c-5598-8326-fcf7ee2d0ed6"] :activity/first-step "step-2ccbe3d6-2634-5637-9466-9ccd96f0e3f1" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-2ccbe3d6-2634-5637-9466-9ccd96f0e3f1" :step/id #uuid "2ccbe3d6-2634-5637-9466-9ccd96f0e3f1" :step/content 17592186097292 :step/next "step-33ff57a1-4ad9-5365-8370-762afd29d628" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-33ff57a1-4ad9-5365-8370-762afd29d628" :step/id #uuid "33ff57a1-4ad9-5365-8370-762afd29d628" :step/content 17592186097294 :step/next "step-c74051f2-6f31-5a23-b00a-9ba4cba0db56" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-c74051f2-6f31-5a23-b00a-9ba4cba0db56" :step/id #uuid "c74051f2-6f31-5a23-b00a-9ba4cba0db56" :step/content "question-5f1c0a58-fb01-5814-8e30-7c47e655e50c" :step/next "step-5ae097ca-dfcf-58c0-b026-e053a35b47c0" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-5ae097ca-dfcf-58c0-b026-e053a35b47c0" :step/id #uuid "5ae097ca-dfcf-58c0-b026-e053a35b47c0" :step/content "question-c00bebe5-d517-59a2-a7ee-fce25fbbc516" :step/next "step-403b655a-e00c-5598-8326-fcf7ee2d0ed6" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-403b655a-e00c-5598-8326-fcf7ee2d0ed6" :step/id #uuid "403b655a-e00c-5598-8326-fcf7ee2d0ed6" :step/content "question-948c8637-9616-53cf-93bb-0432892cbe59" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073746 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-05ed837d-3821-5be3-89df-8ca589e409e2" "question-1444bcbd-c7af-503c-a5fd-f72a90d6d77a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-05ed837d-3821-5be3-89df-8ca589e409e2" :question/id #uuid "05ed837d-3821-5be3-89df-8ca589e409e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-14005" :question/problem "Determine the real roots of the cubic equation $10{y}^{3}-y=2{y}^{3}+y.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's rewrite the polynomial equation in the form ${P}_{n}(y)=0.$ To do this, we subtract all the terms from the right-hand side so that the right-hand side becomes $0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10{y}^{3}-y & =2{y}^{3}+y \\\\ 8{y}^{3}-y & =y \\\\ 8{y}^{3}-2y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, notice that all of the terms of the polynomial have a common factor of $2y.$ We can factor out the $2y$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8{y}^{3}-2y & =0 \\\\ 2y(4{y}^{2}-1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we factor the expression $4{y}^{2}-1$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2y(4{y}^{2}-1) & =0 \\\\ 2y(2y+1)(2y-1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, by applying the zero product rule, the solutions are $y=0,$ $z=-\\frac{1}{2},$ and $y=\\frac{1}{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f7f1648e-bfb1-591c-80ea-4405790435c4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f7f1648e-bfb1-591c-80ea-4405790435c4" :answer-field/id #uuid "f7f1648e-bfb1-591c-80ea-4405790435c4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5b1e67e5-bec5-5ea7-bdf3-f27057c7ae46" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1640a20d-e4d1-5015-9cda-627837d66005" "answer-f7dc453a-52bf-5f89-b1b6-01e35d12e5aa" "answer-5b1e67e5-bec5-5ea7-bdf3-f27057c7ae46" "answer-e8cf239b-fa18-5105-96fb-3beeb63f74e4" "answer-0c92523a-b06e-5c14-a2cd-5360c00395b6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1640a20d-e4d1-5015-9cda-627837d66005" :answer/id #uuid "1640a20d-e4d1-5015-9cda-627837d66005" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-2,\\,0,\\,1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f7dc453a-52bf-5f89-b1b6-01e35d12e5aa" :answer/id #uuid "f7dc453a-52bf-5f89-b1b6-01e35d12e5aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{2},\\,0,\\,1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5b1e67e5-bec5-5ea7-bdf3-f27057c7ae46" :answer/id #uuid "5b1e67e5-bec5-5ea7-bdf3-f27057c7ae46" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{2},\\,0,\\,\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e8cf239b-fa18-5105-96fb-3beeb63f74e4" :answer/id #uuid "e8cf239b-fa18-5105-96fb-3beeb63f74e4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{2},\\,0,\\,\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0c92523a-b06e-5c14-a2cd-5360c00395b6" :answer/id #uuid "0c92523a-b06e-5c14-a2cd-5360c00395b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=0,\\,1,\\,\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1444bcbd-c7af-503c-a5fd-f72a90d6d77a" :question/id #uuid "1444bcbd-c7af-503c-a5fd-f72a90d6d77a" :question/math-academy-id "q-38109" :question/problem "Solve for $x$ where $4{x}^{3}+3x=3{x}^{3}-4x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's rewrite the polynomial equation in the form ${P}_{n}(x)=0.$ To do this, we subtract all the terms from the right-hand side so that the right-hand side becomes $0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{3}+3x & =3{x}^{3}-4x \\\\ {x}^{3}+3x & =-4x \\\\ {x}^{3}+7x & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, notice that all of the terms of the polynomial have a common factor of $x.$ We can factor out the $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}+7x & =0 \\\\ x({x}^{2}+7) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${x}^{2}+7=0$ has no real solutions, we cannot factor the expression ${x}^{2}+7$  further.\n\nFinally, by applying the zero product rule, the only solution is $x=0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-156cc421-00b2-50d1-b76f-984736c8cfcd"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-156cc421-00b2-50d1-b76f-984736c8cfcd" :answer-field/id #uuid "156cc421-00b2-50d1-b76f-984736c8cfcd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-055022f7-b555-5b53-bdb6-52590c8cb0bc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4811dac8-5f59-56b0-ac1b-78612918c845" "answer-9cbb051b-e065-53ef-b7cf-9b608ab9119d" "answer-055022f7-b555-5b53-bdb6-52590c8cb0bc" "answer-549aad98-3e4b-5a26-8533-7d549487f2d0" "answer-9807b2dd-bc9a-5693-ad00-0fc00ed47b0d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4811dac8-5f59-56b0-ac1b-78612918c845" :answer/id #uuid "4811dac8-5f59-56b0-ac1b-78612918c845" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-1,\\,0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9cbb051b-e065-53ef-b7cf-9b608ab9119d" :answer/id #uuid "9cbb051b-e065-53ef-b7cf-9b608ab9119d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-1,\\,0,\\,5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-055022f7-b555-5b53-bdb6-52590c8cb0bc" :answer/id #uuid "055022f7-b555-5b53-bdb6-52590c8cb0bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-549aad98-3e4b-5a26-8533-7d549487f2d0" :answer/id #uuid "549aad98-3e4b-5a26-8533-7d549487f2d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=0,\\,3,\\,5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9807b2dd-bc9a-5693-ad00-0fc00ed47b0d" :answer/id #uuid "9807b2dd-bc9a-5693-ad00-0fc00ed47b0d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=0,\\,5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073747 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-9b05fed3-4ab6-51d7-8e10-a90e6b0e2462"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-9b05fed3-4ab6-51d7-8e10-a90e6b0e2462" :question/id #uuid "9b05fed3-4ab6-51d7-8e10-a90e6b0e2462" :question/math-academy-id "q-70466" :question/problem "Find the roots of the polynomial $p(t)=6{t}^{6}+15{t}^{5}+6{t}^{4}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the roots of the polynomial, we must solve the equation $p(t)=0,$ that is\n\n$$\n6{t}^{6}+15{t}^{5}+6{t}^{4}=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that all of the terms of the polynomial have a common factor of $3{t}^{4}.$ We can factor out the $3{t}^{4}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{t}^{4}(2{t}^{2}+5t+2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we factor the expression $2{t}^{2}+5t+2$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{t}^{4}(2{t}^{2}+5t+2) & =0 \\\\ 3{t}^{4}(2t+1)(t+2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, by applying the zero product rule, the solutions are $t=0,$ $t=-\\frac{1}{2},$ and $t=-2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-18396988-80bb-5ded-8e95-066e394e22f6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-18396988-80bb-5ded-8e95-066e394e22f6" :answer-field/id #uuid "18396988-80bb-5ded-8e95-066e394e22f6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7d7dfd6f-3f62-5676-8e59-619b7bf533ae" :answer-field/choices ["answer-968b97e4-e536-5306-8c56-99b308114e5c" "answer-7d7dfd6f-3f62-5676-8e59-619b7bf533ae" "answer-a2cdcfa6-1b3f-5b11-8574-abd7c13b156b" "answer-1c64f283-376a-5aea-ad5b-0fd0b69f4c0a" "answer-dce9f8d9-a244-590c-93fe-5a247b012a8e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-968b97e4-e536-5306-8c56-99b308114e5c" :answer/id #uuid "968b97e4-e536-5306-8c56-99b308114e5c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=-2,\\,-1,\\,1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7d7dfd6f-3f62-5676-8e59-619b7bf533ae" :answer/id #uuid "7d7dfd6f-3f62-5676-8e59-619b7bf533ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=-2,\\,-\\frac{1}{2},\\,0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a2cdcfa6-1b3f-5b11-8574-abd7c13b156b" :answer/id #uuid "a2cdcfa6-1b3f-5b11-8574-abd7c13b156b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=-2,\\,0,\\,1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1c64f283-376a-5aea-ad5b-0fd0b69f4c0a" :answer/id #uuid "1c64f283-376a-5aea-ad5b-0fd0b69f4c0a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=-4,\\,-1,\\,0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dce9f8d9-a244-590c-93fe-5a247b012a8e" :answer/id #uuid "dce9f8d9-a244-590c-93fe-5a247b012a8e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=-6,\\,-\\frac{3}{2},\\,0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-3feed6d1-a0d5-5ab7-9ea2-a3df2bac